# Build context for images built from the repo root. Only frontend/Dockerfile.runtime does that (docker-compose.prod.yml
# web service); every other image has its own context (backend, source-sim, frontend) and its own .dockerignore.
# Allow-list: everything is out except the web app's sources and the demo it extracts its stylesheet and photos from.
*
!frontend
!fixtures/demo

# inside the allowed folders: secrets, dependencies, build output, generated files (the build regenerates them), tests
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/node_modules
frontend/dist
frontend/src/styles/legacy.gen.css
frontend/public/assets/products
frontend/*.tsbuildinfo
frontend/coverage
frontend/e2e
frontend/playwright-report
frontend/test-results
frontend/**/*.test.ts
frontend/**/*.test.tsx
frontend/.dockerignore
frontend/Dockerfile*
